    "consulting_editor": "Amie Koenig •Histologic lesions in brain—mild, multifocal, nonsuppurative meningo encephalitis (lymphocytic to lymphohistiocytic perivascular infiltrates predominantly in gray matter). TREATMENT Supportive therapy for neurologic abnormalities. MEDICATIONS •Antiviral drugs have not been tested for efficacy. •Antipyretics may decrease fever. •Anticonvulsant medications, as indicated. FOLLOW-UP PREVENTION/AVOIDANCE Vaccines available for horses, have not been approved for dogs. MISCELLANEOUS ZOONOTIC POTENTIAL •West Nile virus can infect numerous species including humans; however, the insect vector is generally necessary for transmission and the viremia is too low in infected dogs to serve as host for infecting feeding mosquitoes. dogs and cats. Vet Clin Small Anim 2008, 38:863–878.",
